  "description": "The deployment consists of three containers. The **web** container, named **web_container**, runs the **nginx:latest** image on the **frontend** network. It exposes HTTP and HTTPS by mapping host ports\u202f80\u219280 and\u202f443\u2192443, and mounts the site source with a read\u2011only bind\u202f`/var/www/html:/usr/share/nginx/html:ro`. Its runtime environment sets `NODE_ENV=production` and `API_URL=http://api.local`. The service is configured to always restart, carries the label `com.example.description=Web server`, and uses Google\u2019s DNS servers\u202f8.8.8.8 and\u202f8.8.4.4. For internal resolution it adds two extra hosts:\u202f`host1`\u202f\u2192\u202f192.168.1.10 and\u202f`host2`\u202f\u2192\u202f192.168.1.11.\n\nThe **db** service is built from the local directory **./db** using **Dockerfile.mysql**, and the resulting container is called **db_container**. It receives the environment variables `MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=secret` and `MYSQL_DATABASE=appdb`, and persists data with a volume mapping `/var/lib/mysql:/var/lib/mysql`. Memory is limited to **512\u202fm**, with a swap ceiling of **1\u202fg**, and the container will restart on failure up to five times (`on-failure:5`). Logging is handled by the **json\u2011file** driver, writing to `/var/log/docker.log`, and the MySQL port\u202f3306 is exposed directly.\n\nFinally, the **proxy** service extends the **web** definition from the same `docker-compose.yml` file. It runs in a container named **proxy_container**, forwards host port\u202f8080 to the web service\u2019s port\u202f80, and operates in transparent mode via the environment variable `PROXY_MODE=transparent`."
